From 2f8b2704e2913fab260b55cd14d22bcd918b56cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 15:08:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/22] fix(projects): public projects share chats and
 knowledge only; going public needs the typed name

Bug: making a project public handed every active user the full "viewer"
capability set, so memory items, the media library, the member roster,
pending invitations (with tokens), the invite picker (a directory of all
users) and the active config with its custom prompt were readable by anyone
in the organization. The turn planner also injected project memory into a
public viewer's chat, where the model would repeat it. The visibility flip
itself was one unguarded PUT.

Change:
- New read capabilities chat.read, resource.read, memory.read, media.read,
  members.read, config.read. Every member role has all of them; the implicit
  public viewer has only project.view, chat.read, resource.read.
- Memory list, media list/get/download, attach-from-media, active config,
  member roster -> the matching read capability (403 for public viewers).
  Invitations and the invitable-users picker -> member.manage.
- plan_project_turn injects project memory only when the caller can
  memory.read; the custom prompt still shapes the public viewer's chat.
- update_project(visibility="public") requires confirm_public_name equal
  to the *current* project name (typed confirmation verified server-side)
  and writes a project.visibility.public audit event.
- Frontend: non-members no longer see the media/members/settings tabs; the
  make-public dialog asks for the project name and sends it along.

Tests: tests/test_projects_public_scope.py (outsider vs viewer-member matrix,
memory not injected for outsiders, typed confirmation + audit). Two existing
tests aligned with the new policy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
